 rest-fiber representation with $P^\mu=(M,0,0,0)$, $M>0$, scalar central charges $Z^{12}=zI$ and $Z^{21}=-zI$, and a common dense invariant domain $\mathcal D$ on which the supercharges, their actual Hilbert adjoints, and every product below are defined. Thus $P_0=-M$, each supercharge has mass dimension one-half, and $M,z$ have mass dimension one. Choose $\phi\in\mathbb R$ so that $e^{-i\phi}z=|z|$, with arbitrary $\phi$ when $z=0$, and on $\mathcal D$ put
+
+$$q=Q^1_1,\qquad r=Q^2_2,\qquad A=q-e^{i\phi}r^*,\qquad A^\sharp=q^*-e^{-i\phi}r.$$
+
+For every $\psi\in\mathcal D$,
+
+$$\langle(AA^\sharp+A^\sharp A)\psi,\psi\rangle=\|A\psi\|^2+\|A^\sharp\psi\|^2=4(M-|z|)\|\psi\|^2.$$
+
+Consequently, for every nonzero $\psi\in\mathcal D$, $M=|z|$ if and only if $A\psi=A^\sharp\psi=0$. The operator $A^\sharp$ is the displayed sum of the individual charge adjoints; for unbounded charges it is not asserted to be the maximal-domain adjoint of the sum $A$. This conditional statement neither asserts that such a vector or representation occurs in a physical model nor proves its dynamical stability.
+
+## Statement references
+
+[Bilal, §3.4](https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0101055)
+
+[Tong, §2.4.2](https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/supersymmetric-field-theory/susy2.pdf)
+
+[[thm-qftx-n-extended-central-charge-bounds]]
+
+[[def-qftx-unitary-super-poincare-representation]]
+
+[[def-countable-choice]]
+
+## Facts & Assumptions
+
+**Given:** The stated massive rest-fiber data and $\psi\in\mathcal D$.
+
+[A1] Assume $\mathrm{AC}_\omega$, as required by the exact unbounded-operator and representation suppliers ([[def-countable-choice]]): for every sequence of nonempty sets there is a choice function selecting one element from each set.
+
+[F1] [[thm-qftx-n-extended-central-charge-bounds]]: in the $N=2$ rest fiber, $\{q,q^*\}=\{r,r^*\}=2MI$, $\{q,r\}=2zI$, $\{r^*,q^*\}=2\bar zI$, and $AA^\sharp+A^\sharp A=4(M-|z|)I$ on the common product domain; at $M=|z|$ the two displayed combinations annihilate every vector in that domain.
+
+[F2] [[def-qftx-unitary-super-poincare-representation]]: the Hilbert inner product is positive and linear in its first variable; each charge adjoint is its actual Hilbert adjoint; the common dense invariant domain is contained in the domains of all generator products in the algebra.
+
+## Proof
+
+**Proof technique:** direct.
+
+**Given:** [A1], [F1], [F2], and the operators in the Statement.
+
+1.1 Expanding $\|A\psi\|^2+\|A^\sharp\psi\|^2$ gives $\|q\psi\|^2+\|r^*\psi\|^2+\|q^*\psi\|^2+\|r\psi\|^2-2\operatorname{Re}(e^{-i\phi}\langle q\psi,r^*\psi\rangle)-2\operatorname{Re}(e^{i\phi}\langle q^*\psi,r\psi\rangle)$. Expanding $AA^\sharp+A^\sharp A$ gives the same four diagonal terms. Its cross terms are $-e^{-i\phi}(qr+rq)-e^{i\phi}(r^*q^*+q^*r^*)$; the actual-adjoint identities $\langle qr\psi,\psi\rangle=\langle r\psi,q^*\psi\rangle$, $\langle rq\psi,\psi\rangle=\langle q\psi,r^*\psi\rangle$, $\langle r^*q^*\psi,\psi\rangle=\langle q^*\psi,r\psi\rangle$, and $\langle q^*r^*\psi,\psi\rangle=\langle r^*\psi,q\psi\rangle$ pair these terms into exactly the two negative real parts above. The common product-domain hypothesis makes each identity legitimate, so $\langle(AA^\sharp+A^\sharp A)\psi,\psi\rangle=\|A\psi\|^2+\|A^\sharp\psi\|^2$. [F2, given, algebra]
+
+1.2 By [F1], the left side in step 1.1 equals $4(M-|z|)\|\psi\|^2$, so $4(M-|z|)\|\psi\|^2=\|A\psi\|^2+\|A^\sharp\psi\|^2$ for every $\psi\in\mathcal D$. This is an identity of nonnegative squared norms. [A1, F1, step 1.1]
+
+2.1 If $\psi\ne0$ and $A\psi=A^\sharp\psi=0$, step 1.2 gives $4(M-|z|)\|\psi\|^2=0$. Since $\|\psi\|^2>0$, division by $4\|\psi\|^2$ yields $M=|z|$. [given, step 1.2, algebra]
+
+2.2 If $M=|z|$, then [F1] gives $A\psi=A^\sharp\psi=0$ for every $\psi\in\mathcal D$. Together with step 2.1 this proves both directions for every nonzero domain vector. [F1, step 2.1] ∎
