The required page supplier qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model has no current page/item carrier. Its exact planned postulate contract was inspected: it selects the actual global gauge group, bundle sector, metric, invariant pairing, matter, units, coupling, action, boundary conditions, and scope; it is an adopted classical model, not a theorem or a continuum-QFT existence claim. The A-page requires edge remains open in the cross-batch file. No Yang-Mills premise is falsely inserted into the BPS definition or algebra-only examples.

## Finite checks and validation state

A one-off Node matrix check at M=1 verified every mixed and central bracket for the explicit 4x4 short module, its null combination, and every mixed/same-chirality bracket for the explicit 16x16 long module. It is recorded in the proof contracts as a bounded finite algebra check, not as a general proof, full Poincare representation, or registered finite-smoke gate.

Scoped prechecks, proof-layout, contract, render, dependency, and content-policy results are appended after the final runs. Readiness remains escalated wherever a current required in-run readiness record is absent; completion records do not confer independent proof acceptance.
